
--> @Operation
    is used to document individual API endpoints.
    While OpenAPI can auto-detect endpoints, @Operation adds human-readable meaning to each API.

    What It Describes
    @Operation explains:
    What the endpoint does
    Why it exists
    How it should be used
    This is extremely important because method names alone are not enough for API consumers.


    Why @Operation Matters
    Improves API clarity
    Reduces dependency on external documentation
    Helps frontend and QA teams understand intent
    Makes Swagger UI self-explanatory
    From an interview perspective:
    @Operation improves API discoverability and usability

